title: "Lean LFM-to-Dirac Derivation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "G. D."
version: "0.13.0-research"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanDiracDerivation"
license: CC0-1.0
abstract: >-
  A noncanonical Lean 4 research derivation through DIRAC-013. It connects a
  positive two-field C19 action to a cubical continuum square root and maps
  both native rank-four copies to the conventional Dirac representation. It
  derives both frequency graphs, selects the nonnegative rest coefficient,
  bounds continuum evolution, and derives the positive-frequency density and
  current limit from the native action. Physical spin and an electron remain
  open.
